                <pb facs="0671" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg665"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. von Holleben.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I inclose herewith the
                    copy of the dispatch (No. 240) from our acting consul-general at Samoa which I
                    promised in our interview this morning.</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
